* Option file 3 for CPLEX solver - dual simplex with warm start enabled.
* To use with CPLEX, set '$Setglobal USEOPTIONFILE 3' in balgams.opt, or pass --USEOPTIONFILE=3 on the gams command line.
*
* Unlike op2/op4 (barrier, advind 0, which explicitly discards any previous solution), this uses
* dual simplex so a later solve can warm-start from a previous run's basis via execute_loadpoint.
* This is needed for scenarios whose fullyear solve is certain to exceed a single job's HPC wall-time
* and must resume across a chain of resubmissions instead of restarting from scratch each time.
* See docs/adr/0001-warm-start-fullyear-timeout.md.
*
* "LPmethod  2": Dual simplex.
* "advind  1": Use the previous/loaded solution as an advanced (warm) start.
* "Threads  -1": Use all available threads except 1. If memory tight, set the Threads parameter to 1.

LPmethod  2
advind 1
